	quest.562807A2687B3DEF.quest_desc: [
		"It can be found in the structures of the main world (churches, master cartographers and villagers have a probability of refreshing the structure map) and can also be refreshed in the wild."
		""
		"&8Hostile to the demon race and neutral to non-demon races&r"
		"If you don't have strong skills or magic, please don't try to challenge her!"
		"{image:ablazeaqzlcz:textures/ftb/hinata_sakaguchi.png width:60 height:60 align:center}"
		"&lBOSS stage explanation:&r"
		""
		"&lfirst stage&r"
		"&6-Summon 5 high-level elves and enter the \"rift field mode\"."
		"&6-After the High Elf is defeated, Hinata will enter the second stage.&r&r"
		""
		"&lsecond stage&r"
		"&6-At this stage, Hinata only uses passive skills, and attacks with \"Colorful Final Thorn Assault\", while also performing a small amount of teleportation."
		"&6-Enter phase three when her HP drops below 75%.&r"
		""
		"&lThe third stage&r"
		"&5At this stage, Hinata will continue to use sword skills and simultaneously perform: Hellfire, Blizzard, Earth Prison, and Sky Cutting Skills&r"
		"&6-When her HP drops below 50%, she will start casting \"Atomic Crash\":"
		" &6-During casting, the target's movement speed will be slowed down."
		" &6-To cancel this Skill, you need to cause enough damage to her."
		" &6-If \"Atomic Collapse\" hits the target, the target will be killed instantly."
		" &6- When HP drops to 25%, she will enter the fourth stage."
		""
		"&lStage 4&r"
		"&6-When entering this phase, Hinata is restored to 50% HP and that becomes her new maximum health (yellow bar)."
		"&6-Her passive health regeneration rate increased to:"
		"&6-Restores 10 Health + 50 Mental Health per second"
		"&6-In this stage, Hinata will use all the Skills from the previous stages and additionally equip: (Holy Spirit Arms) (Moonlight Rapier)"
		"&6-Melting Slash Effect: -When hitting the target, it will ignore armor, resistance and defense reduction, and directly cause 3000 damage."
	]
	quest.562807A2687B3DEF.quest_subtitle: "Hinata Sakaguchi"
	quest.562807A2687B3DEF.title: "\"Good luck\""
	quest.5631F6ECD23395D2.quest_desc: [
		"There is a probability that the Boss will be refreshed in the wild."
		""
		"&8Hostile to the Demon race and non-Human races, and neutral to the Human race&r"
		"&8Hostile to creatures with an EP of more than 10,000&r"
		"If you don't have strong skills or magic, please don't try to challenge him!"
		""
		"&lBOSS stage explanation:&r"
		""
		"&lfirst stage&r"
		"&6-Use melee and ranged Aura attacks."
		"&6-Has a 15% dodge chance and may teleport to the target when attacked."
		"&6-Skills available: Aura Slash, Elephant Step Aura Bullet."
		"&6-Restore 12 health points + 60 soul health points per second."
		"&6-When his HP is below 50%, enter the second stage.&r"
		""
		"&lThe second stage (Beast King form)&r"
		"&6-When entering this stage, Karion will fully recover HP, Magicule, and Aura, and clear all negative effects."
		"&6-Acquire the ability to fly."
		"&6-Dodge chance increased to 30%."
		"&6-The armor value is increased by 20 points, the attack power is increased by 20 points, and the knockback resistance is increased by 0.2."
		"&6-Her passive health regeneration rate is reduced to: 4 health points + 20 soul health points per second."
		"&6-At this stage, Karion will use all the Skills from the first stage and gain stronger mobility."
	]
	quest.5631F6ECD23395D2.quest_subtitle: "I heard you are crazy"
	quest.5631F6ECD23395D2.title: "Strong melee fighter"
	quest.56413501A9E9D8FC.quest_desc: [
		"&6Players will initially have 0 points of Dwarf Reputation (DR for short)."
		""
		"1. When you attack any dwarf, as long as there is another untamed dwarf nearby (that is, there is a witness) you will lose 0.1 DR."
		""
		"2. When you kill any dwarf, as long as there is another untamed dwarf nearby, you will lose 1DR."
		""
		"3. When you kill a monster that is attacking a dwarf (that is, save the dwarf), you will receive 1DR."
		""
		"4. Each time you upgrade the trading level of a dwarf merchant, you will receive 0.1 DR."
		""
		"5. Each time you make a purchase transaction (purchase items with gold coins) you will receive 0.05 DR."
		""
		"6. Each time you perform a sales transaction (sell items to get gold coins) you will receive 0.01 DR."
		""
		"&6If your DR is positive, the dwarves will trade with you at a 0.5% discount per point."
		"&6If your DR is negative, the dwarves will trade with you at a price increase of 2% per point.&r"
	]
	quest.56413501A9E9D8FC.quest_subtitle: "Don't cause trouble!"
	quest.56413501A9E9D8FC.title: "Dwarf Reputation System"
	quest.565894017692BCC7.quest_desc: [
		"&lResistance Acquisition Guide&r"
		""
		"Resistances are divided into different levels based on acquisition difficulty: Easy / Medium / Hard. Each difficulty has different requirements."
		"&lEasy:&r Taking more than 5 damage in a single hit grants 1 Learning Point. Requires 350 points to fully learn."
		"&lMedium:&r Taking more than 15 damage in a single hit grants 1 Learning Point. Requires 500 points to fully learn."
		"&lHard:&r Taking more than 20 damage in a single hit grants 1 Learning Point. Requires 700 points to fully learn."
		""
		"The default difficulty of each resistance is as follows:"
		"&lEasy:&r Corrosion, Poison, and Paralysis."
		"&lMedium:&r Pain, Pierce, Natural Attacks, and Holy Attacks. Natural Attacks include the 7 major elements, Gravity, Lightning, Heat, and Cold."
		"&lHard:&r Physical Attacks, Magic, Spiritual Attacks, and Abnormal Status."
		""
		"Resistances can also be learned from damage below the damage threshold."
		"Damage below the threshold accumulates. When the accumulated value reaches 10 times the threshold damage, 1 Learning Point is gained."
		"For example, Physical Attack Resistance requires taking more than 20 damage in a single hit to gain 1 Learning Point."
		"If the player takes less than 20 damage, such as 12 damage, the skill does not immediately gain a Learning Point. Instead, it gains 12 \"Damage Points\". When these points accumulate to 200, which is 20 x 10, the skill gains 1 Learning Point."
		"Whenever the skill gains 1 Learning Point, its \"Damage Points\" reset to 0."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"What should we do if a creature has resistance?"
		"For the most troublesome example, Physical Resistance, the solution is simple: switch to elemental or magical damage. Physical Resistance only blocks physical damage, so Fire skills and magic attacks are completely unaffected."
	]
